                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is actually plain stupid.\nNo sense at all.\nIt's RPG Maker and the graphics are also extremely nice to me, but there's nothing else apart from the graphics.\nIt's a clicker. You click multiple times on the doors and they break down, hence the title of the game.\nIf you're a lover like me of '90s JRPGs ported on GBA and such you'll find very pleasant artworks, but it's completely nonsense since there is no plot!\nYou travel alone with your character through maps and you only have to click on doors.\nAnd it is random, so some doors will take like 50 or 100 clicks. Or way more!!\nI don't know if the maps are also random, but I found myself through small maps one after the other.\nIt's all very annoying, since you don't even have animations or battles, you just click on doors.\nWhere after 100 clicks a bubble will tell you that there's the need of a key, it means that you just have to click on your left and nothing else. So you can play this almost by idling.\nI really think that this is one of the worst games on Steam.",
